-- title:
--   Serre–Tate lifting of an abelian scheme along its formal group
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a commutative Artinian local ring $B$ whose residue field is algebraically closed, and a commutative $B$-algebra $B_0$ such that $B \to B_0$ is surjective with nilpotent kernel; assume $q$ is nilpotent in $B$. Let $f_0 : A_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_0$ be a morphism of schemes carrying a relative group law $L_0$ (a group structure, natural in the base, on the sections of $f_0$ over any $B_0$-scheme) which is commutative, and satisfying the bundle of conditions that $f_0$ is smooth and proper, has connected fibres and admits a relative group law. Let $F$ be a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law over $B$, and $\theta_0$ an assignment, to each $B_0$-algebra $B'$ and each pair of elements of $B'$, of a section of $f_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B'$, which is formal coordinates for $L_0$ with respect to the reduction of $F$ to $B_0$: it is compatible with $B_0$-algebra maps on nilpotent tuples and, for every $B'$ and every ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1} = 0$, it restricts to a bijection from $J$-tuples onto the $J$-infinitesimal sections (those dying modulo $J$) carrying the $n$-truncated law $F$ to multiplication in $L_0$. Assume further that the $q$-power torsion of $L_0$ is infinitesimal: for every $B_0$-algebra $C$, every $m$ and every section $P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $q^m P$ the unit, there is a nilpotent ideal $J \subseteq C$ with $P$ $J$-infinitesimal; and that $F$ has height $4$ at every residue field: for each field $k$ and each surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to k$, the $k$-dimension of $k[[X_1,X_2]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the components of the $q$-fold iterate $[q]$ of the law $F \otimes_\rho k$ equals $q^4$. Then there exists a bare deformation $D$ of $(f_0, L_0)$ over $B$ — a scheme $A$ with $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} B$, a commutative relative group law $L$ on $f$, the same smooth/proper/connected-fibres bundle for $f$, and a morphism $g : A_0 \to A$ making the square over $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec} B_0$ cartesian and compatible with the two multiplications — together with formal coordinates $\theta$ for $D.L$ in dimension $2$ whose associated formal group law is exactly $F$, and which lift $\theta_0$: for every ring $B''$ that is an algebra over both $B$ and $B_0$ compatibly, and every pair of nilpotent elements $s$ of $B''$, the section $\theta_0(s)$ followed by $g$ equals $\theta(s)$.
--
--   This is the essential-surjectivity half of the Serre–Tate theorem in its bare form (no endomorphisms or level structure), at Artinian local base points with algebraically closed residue field: an abelian scheme with infinitesimal $q$-power torsion lifts along any prescribed lift of its formal group. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, to lift fake elliptic curves together with their special formal module structures.
